# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# منارة — مكتب التطوير التربوي · environment template (PostgreSQL/Neon)
#
# Copy to .env and fill the values. NEVER commit the real .env.
# Never paste real credentials into chat, issues, or logs.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1) DATABASE_URL — POOLED connection (application runtime).
#    Neon Console → your project → "Connection string" → select
#    "Pooled connection". It looks like:
#      postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-XXXX-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/DBNAME?sslmode=require
#    For Prisma + PgBouncer compatibility append pgbouncer=true and a
#    small connection_limit:
#      &pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=5
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-XXXX-pooler.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require&pgbouncer=true&connection_limit=5"

# 2) DIRECT_DATABASE_URL — DIRECT (non-pooled) connection.
#    Same project, WITHOUT "-pooler" in the host. Used ONLY by Prisma
#    Migrate (migrate deploy / diff / studio) — DDL must bypass the
#    pooler. Also used by the data-transfer script.
DIRECT_DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-XXXX.REGION.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"

# 3) Auth secret — generate a NEW strong value for production:
#    node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(48).toString('hex'))"
AUTH_SECRET="generate-a-new-64+-char-random-hex-string"

# 4) Email delivery mode (ethereal = catch-all test inbox, no real mail).
#    For production mail set smtp + credentials in the dashboard, never here.
EMAIL_MODE="ethereal"

# 5) Local assignment-file storage (local dev only).
#    NOTE: Vercel's filesystem is read-only — production needs an
#    external store (S3-compatible). Tracked as a known limitation.
ASSIGNMENTS_STORAGE_DIR="./.data/assignment-files"